{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X_s$", "MATH_0002": "$x'$", "MATH_0003": "$x$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_s, x}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_s, x'}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_s, x}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_s, x'}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-tr-deg-specialization}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:eeba08fe5a55b4cf61269d57f09213725390ef1864dc6305d716ae2850231362", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f8ffb4d3f18ed4b1a13f59fb16a48ac22711df8327aea38d2b68d367c463f676", "source_text": "Part (1) follows from the fact that any open of <MATH_0001> containing <MATH_0002>\nalso contains <MATH_0003>. Part (2) follows since <MATH_0004> is a\nlocalization of <MATH_0005> at a prime ideal, hence any chain\nof prime ideals in <MATH_0006> is part of a strictly longer\nchain of primes in <MATH_0007>. The last inequality follows from\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f5d67a2cf9244b00ab61ece99984e09332abc17dcfffb85cde09adb6e86d0a43", "unit_id": "tag:06RU:proof"}
